{"step_index":1900,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T02:24:28Z","input_tokens":2873,"cache_read_tokens":242511,"output_tokens":3837,"thinking":"The chapter extraction logic appears to use a regular expression to identify chapter titles based on a pattern starting with \"Chapter\" followed by a number. This works for the main chapters. Considering the presence of appendices in the file, it's necessary to expand the chapter identification to also recognize these sections based on the \"Appendix\" naming convention.\n\n\nExamining the EPUB file structure, it's clear the OPF spine defines the intended reading order, which should be prioritized over directory scanning for chapter extraction. This guarantees the correct sequence of chapters, even in complex books. This is a solid approach.\n\n\n\nThe code now locates the OPF file within the EPUB structure to determine the book's intended reading order via the spine. This involves parsing the OPF XML to extract manifest items and item references to construct the chapter sequence. If the OPF file is not found, it falls back to a directory scan, but this will be used as a last resort. The image files are also copied into the illustration directory.\n\n\nThe code iterates through files in the temporary directory, prioritizing HTML/XHTML files and sorting them for reading order. File names are checked against a blacklist to exclude introductory content. HTML tags are cleaned from the text, including the extraction of image sources and specific structural elements. The extracted clean text includes images, subtitles, headings and paragraphs.\n\n\nThe text extraction logic now incorporates several checks to identify chapter titles with greater accuracy. Initially, lines are split, trimmed, and filtered to remove empty lines and book titles from chapter identification. The code then attempts to match chapter titles using a regex pattern, considering variations in numbering. If the initial regex fails, it searches for explicit \"Chapter\" markers within the lines to derive the title from subsequent lines.\n\nFallback mechanisms are used. If no chapter markers are found, it looks for specific phrases and uses the filename or the first few lines of the text as a default. Finally, the extracted data is structured into chapter objects, and the temporary directory is removed after processing.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"const fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst { execSync } = require('child_process');\n\nconst epubPath = 'd:/JV/novel yoga/1_Dune_-_Frank_Herbert.epub';\nconst tempDir = path.join(path.dirname(epubPath), '.temp_test_dune_final');\nif (fs.existsSync(tempDir)) fs.rmSync(tempDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\nfs.mkdirSync(tempDir, { recursive: true });\nexecSync(`tar -xf \"${epubPath}\" -C \"${tempDir}\"`, { stdio: 'pipe' });\n\nfunction findOpf(dir) {\n  for (const ent of fs.readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n    const full = path.join(dir, ent.name);\n    if (ent.isDirectory()) {\n      const res = findOpf(full);\n      if (res) return res;\n    } else if (ent.name.endsWith('.opf')) {\n      return full;\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nconst opfFile = findOpf(tempDir);\nconst spineHrefs = [];\nlet opfDir = tempDir;\n\nif (opfFile) {\n  opfDir = path.dirname(opfFile);\n  const opfXml = fs.readFileSync(opfFile, 'utf-8');\n  const manifest = {};\n  for (const itemTag of opfXml.match(/<item\\b[^>]*>/gi) || []) {\n    const idM = itemTag.match(/\\bid=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']/i);\n    const hrefM = itemTag.match(/\\bhref=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']/i);\n    if (idM && hrefM) {\n      manifest[idM[1]] = hrefM[1];\n    }\n  }\n  const itemrefs = [...opfXml.matchAll(/<itemref\\b[^>]*\\bidref=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']/gi)].map(m => m[1]);\n  for (const idref of itemrefs) {\n    if (manifest[idref]) spineHrefs.push(manifest[idref]);\n  }\n}\n\nconst chapters = [];\nconst targetFiles = spineHrefs.map(href => path.resolve(opfDir, href));\n\nfor (const full of targetFiles) {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(full)) continue;\n  const fname = path.basename(full);\n  if (/cover|alsobyauthor|copyright|title\\.xhtml|dedication|next-reads|nav\\.xhtml|frontmatter/i.test(fname)) continue;\n\n  const html = fs.readFileSync(full, 'utf-8');\n  let cleanText = html\n    .replace(/<script\\b[^<]*(?:(?!<\\/script>)<[^<]*)*<\\/script>/gi, '')\n    .replace(/<style\\b[^<]*(?:(?!<\\/style>)<[^<]*)*<\\/style>/gi, '')\n    .replace(/<img[^>]+src=['\"]([^'\"]+)['\"][^>]*>/gi, (m, src) => `\\n\\n[[ILUSTRASI:${path.basename(src)}]]\\n\\n`)\n    .replace(/<h[1-6][^>]*>(.*?)<\\/h[1-6]>/gi, '\\n\\n# $1\\n')\n    .replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '\\n')\n    .replace(/\\n\\s*\\n/g, '\\n\\n')\n    .trim();\n\n  if (cleanText.length > 200) {\n    const lines = cleanText.split('\\n').map(l => l.trim()).filter(l => Boolean(l) && !/^(The\\s+Hobbit|Dune)\\s*$/i.test(l));\n    const firstRealLine = lines[0] || '';\n    if (/^(CONTENTS|TABLE OF CONTENTS|LIST OF ILLUSTRATIONS|NOTE ON THE TEXT|WORKS BY|COPYRIGHT|PRAISE FOR)\\b/i.test(firstRealLine)) continue;\n\n    let title = '';\n    const duneChMatch = firstRealLine.match(/^Chapter\\s+([0-9]+)(?:,\\s*Dune)?/i);\n    if (duneChMatch) {\n      title = `Chapter ${duneChMatch[1]}`;\n    } else {\n      const chIdx = lines.findIndex(l => /^Chapter\\b/i.test(l));\n      if (chIdx !== -1) {\n        const chNum = lines[chIdx + 1] || '';\n        const chName = lines[chIdx + 2] || '';\n        title = `Chapter ${chNum}: ${chName}`;\n      } else if (/Author[’']s Note/i.test(html) || /languages and letters/i.test(html)) {\n        title = \"Catatan Penulis (Author's Note: Runes & Languages)\";\n      } else {\n        for (const l of lines.slice(0, 5)) {\n          const cleanL = l.replace(/^#+\\s*/, '').trim();\n          if (/^(Chapter|Bab|Part|Book|Appendix)\\b/i.test(cleanL)) {\n            title = cleanL;\n            break;\n          }\n        }\n        if (!title) {\n          title = lines.slice(0, 2).map(l => l.replace(/^#+\\s*/, '').trim()).join(' - ') || fname;\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\n    chapters.push({\n      id: path.basename(full, path.extname(full)),\n      title,\n      chars: cleanText.length\n    });\n  }\n}\n\nfs.rmSync(tempDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\nconsole.log('Total extracted spine chapters:', chapters.length);\nchapters.forEach((c, i) => {\n  if (i < 5 || i >= chapters.length - 8) {\n    console.log(`  [${i+1}] ${c.id} (${c.chars} chars): ${c.title}`);\n  } else if (i === 5) {\n    console.log('  ... and Chapter 06 to 48 ...');\n  }\n});\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\Eevyx\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\dfaefe40-f699-4276-8717-cb4f8030016c\\scratch\\test_dune_spine.js"}}]}
